cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use LaraIoT in your research or software project, please cite it as follows."
type: software
title: "LaraIoT: A Laravel Package for Monitoring and Controlling IoT Devices"
abstract: >-
  LaraIoT is a demonstrative and extensible Laravel package for developing
  web applications for monitoring and controlling IoT devices.
  The package integrates MQTT communication, device and topic management,
  device state persistence, and command publishing.
  It supports two alternative mechanisms for updating data in the web
  interface: periodic HTTP polling and WebSockets, enabling developers
  and researchers to explore and compare these approaches.
  LaraIoT offers a frontend-agnostic installation and an optional web
  interface built with Vue.js and Inertia.
  It provides a reusable starting point for developing IoT monitoring
  and control applications with Laravel.
  The package is intended for research, education, and prototyping.
  Security hardening is outside its scope, and additional safeguards
  are required before deployment in production environments.
repository-code: "https://github.com/danielpopa26/laraiot"
